    {
      "evidence": "publication_queue.py:608-611 computes `resolved_handoff = ... _admission_handoff(root, branch, expected_head)` unconditionally, ahead of `_events`/`_admission` at 612-613. It is consumed only at line 658, and only when `current.get('task_identity') is None or current.get('head') != expected_head`. D4 and the \"Managed proof unavailable\" scenario require failure before mutations, so this ordering is defensible. It does mean a no-op re-admission can now raise where it previously succeeded. The delta spec and design do not say whether that is intended.",
      "id": "admit-eager-handoff-on-readmission",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "`admit` now resolves the managed handoff before it checks whether the PR is already admitted. A retry or idempotent re-admission of a managed candidate can therefore fail provenance, for example when the coordinator checkout is not at the admitted head. Before this change the handoff was computed lazily and only when a transition was actually needed."
    }
